{
  "_comment": "Declarative vessel inventory for the substrate image. apply-inventory.sh reads this at boot (before systemd) to select which units run, so one image runs any SUBSET: a full local substrate, a minimal hub (store+control+api+transport), or a compute-only spoke. DEFAULT (no ENABLED_ROLES/ENABLED_VESSELS env) = every unit enabled, identical to today. Selection env: ENABLED_ROLES=comma,roles | ENABLED_VESSELS=comma,units (explicit, overrides roles) | DISABLED_VESSELS=comma,units (always off). Per-vessel fork remotes: repo_owner_default (or per-vessel repo_owner) + the `repo` field feed setup-git-push.sh / clone-vessel-repos so a fork can point vessels at its own GitHub org. NAMED PROFILE 'analysis-backend' (the minimum backend a white-labelled metabob-mcp client attaches to = discovery + concept-db + analysis-vessel + activity-api + store/identity/seed/infra deps) is not a role-group here because concept-db/analysis-vessel share the coarse 'compute' role; it is expressed as an explicit ENABLED_VESSELS list in scripts/substrate/deploy-analysis-backend.sh \u2014 keep that list in sync with the units below.",
  "repo_owner_default": "AviGopal",
  "branch_default": "dev",
  "roles": {
    "hub": [
      "store",
      "control",
      "api",
      "transport",
      "seed",
      "infra",
      "registry"
    ],
