      "_comment": "The .service is the unit that actually runs the selection loop; the .timer above only pokes it. apply-inventory.sh masks by exact unit name, so listing only the .timer left boredom-vessel.service ungoverned by role selection — it ran on a hub whose role group excludes compute, where its only dispatch conduit (light-dispatch-vessel.service, compute, correctly masked) was absent. Every dispatch then failed to connect, and the connect-error path records a FAILURE OUTCOME per template, so infrastructure absence was written into the shared learning store as arm quality. Both units must carry the same role.",
      "unit": "boredom-vessel.service",
      "role": "compute",
      "repo": "boredom-vessel"
